# Star vs snowflake — the trade-off

## One dial: how normalized the dimensions are

```
Aspect        Star ★            Snowflake ❄
Dimensions    flat              multi-level
Joins         fewer             more
Query speed   faster            slower
Complexity    low               high
Redundancy    more              less
Storage       more              less
Design        top-down          bottom-up
```

## Which usually wins — the star

- **Storage is cheap; query time & analyst effort are not**
- Simplicity **compounds** — easy SQL, easy BI modelling

## Snowflake only for a reason

- A **huge** dim with a repetitive sub-tree · a **shared** outrigger · a **tooling** rule
